S('ch15','simplified_corrections',r'For small deviations from reference conditions, the correction can be expressed.*?(?=## 15\.5)',r'''For corresponding points at the same flow coefficient and similar Mach/Reynolds conditions on the same machine,

$$\frac{Q_2}{Q_1}=\frac{N_2}{N_1},\qquad\frac{H_2}{H_1}\simeq\left(\frac{N_2}{N_1}\right)^2,\qquad\frac{W_2}{W_1}=\frac{\rho_2}{\rho_1}\frac{Q_2}{Q_1}\frac{H_2}{H_1}\frac{\eta_{p,1}}{\eta_{p,2}}.$$

At fixed speed, head in J/kg is primarily set by tip speed and aerodynamic loading; lowering gas molecular weight does not automatically increase delivered head. The head required for a specified pressure ratio generally increases for a lighter gas at the same temperature. Use the referred map to solve the operating point, then check pressure ratio, speed, surge and power together.

''')
